                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>What is the highest-ROI SEO investment for skincare?</h3>
                                        <p>Silo architecture across concern + ingredient + product + skin-type + routine + budget dimensions. 40-80 silo pages built over 12-18 months compound into durable inbound at CAC 3-5x lower than paid. Content library (100-200 pieces) is second-highest ROI investment.</p>
                                        <h3>How long does skincare SEO take to compound?</h3>
                                        <p>First rankings 60-120 days. Meaningful traffic 4-8 months. Compounding revenue driver from month 12+. By month 24, SEO drives 20-40% of monthly revenue for well-invested brands.</p>
                                        <h3>Which skincare keywords should we target first?</h3>
                                        <p>Long-tail commercial-intent queries first ("niacinamide serum for oily skin under 1000", "retinol for beginners night routine", "vitamin C for pigmentation acne-prone"). Broader category terms ("skincare serums") after 12 months of authority-building.</p>
                                        <h3>What schema should a skincare D2C site deploy?</h3>
                                        <p>Product + Organization + LocalBusiness + BreadcrumbList + FAQPage + Article + Review + AggregateRating. All JSON-LD sitewide. 15-30% impression uplift within 45 days + unlocks AI Overviews + rich results.</p>
                                        <h3>How do we optimise for AI Overviews + ChatGPT + Gemini?</h3>
                                        <p>Answer-first paragraphs, structured lists + tables, semantic headings, entity clarity (named brands + ingredients + certifications), verifiable specifics, llms.txt file. 25-60% additional traffic layer possible within 6-12 months.</p>
                                        <h3>What content cadence is realistic for skincare SEO?</h3>
                                        <p>6-10 pieces / month Growth tier. 4-6 pieces / month Starter tier. Below 4/month, compounding slow. Above 10/month, quality drops without team + editorial scaling.</p>
                                        <h3>How many silo pages does a skincare SEO programme need?</h3>
                                        <p>40-80 silo pages across concern + ingredient + product + skin-type + routine dimensions. Built over 12-18 months. Each with unique content + internal linking + schema.</p>
                                        <h3>How does ITD GrowthLabs approach skincare SEO?</h3>
                                        <p>6-dimension keyword architecture + 40-80 silo pages over 12-18 months + 100-200 content library over 18-24 months + full schema + AI Overviews optimisation + organic-revenue-attributed reporting. See <a href="/industries/digital-marketing-for-skincare-brands.php">skincare vertical page</a>.</p>
